---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Base title="Privacy policy — RECN" description="How RECN handles recordings, notes, diagnostics, and support requests.">
  <Header />
  <main class="simple-page shell" id="main-content">
    <header class="simple-page__header">
      <p class="label">PRIVACY</p>
      <h1>Your recordings. Your devices.</h1>
      <p>Privacy policy for RECN, also called RECN Rec, and this website. Updated September 16, 2026.</p>
    </header>
    <article class="prose privacy-policy" aria-label="RECN privacy policy">
      <p>RECN is developed by Shubham Sinha. For privacy questions or requests, email <a href="mailto:sinhashubham472@gmail.com">sinhashubham472@gmail.com</a>.</p>

      <h2>Recordings, notes, and files</h2>
      <p>RECN stores the audio you record or import, notes, attached images, transcripts, projects, and settings on your device. Metadata can include file names, timestamps, recording settings, and device information. You do not need a RECN account to use the app.</p>
      <p>Recording uses microphone access. Features you choose may also use camera or photo access to attach images, audio-library access to import recordings, Bluetooth access for audio devices, and notifications for recording and playback controls. You can manage these permissions in your device settings.</p>
      <p>Transcription processes audio on your device. Downloading a transcription model connects to Hugging Face, which receives the network information needed to serve that download, such as your IP address. The model download does not upload your recording.</p>

      <h2>Sync and sharing</h2>
      <p>If you pair devices, RECN uses local-network discovery and peer-to-peer connections to exchange your library and related metadata with those devices. Device identifiers and names help identify paired devices. RECN does not provide a hosted cloud recording library.</p>
      <p>Exporting or sharing sends the files you select to the app, person, or destination you choose. Those destinations handle the copies under their own practices. Your operating system may also back up app data, depending on your device and backup settings.</p>

      <h2>Crash and error reports</h2>
      <p>Release builds use Sentry to help diagnose crashes and errors. Crash reporting is on by default. You can turn off <strong>Share crash reports</strong> in the app's Settings under Privacy.</p>
      <p>Reports can contain app and operating-system versions, device characteristics, diagnostic identifiers, stack traces, and recent technical logs. Logs may include file names, local paths, or device and connection details. RECN removes home-directory prefixes from outgoing Dart error text and logs, but this is not a guarantee that every diagnostic field is anonymous. Native crash reports are handled by Sentry's native SDK.</p>
      <p>Recordings, note documents, and photos are not intentionally attached to crash reports. RECN disables Sentry's default personal-information collection and performance tracing. Sentry still processes the network information needed to receive reports. Turning reporting off stops future reporting; it does not automatically remove reports already received.</p>

      <h2>This website and support</h2>
      <p>The website is hosted on GitHub Pages. GitHub processes requests to deliver pages and downloads. The site stores your selected colour theme in your browser's local storage.</p>
      <p>If you sign up for updates, your email address is submitted to Formspree so we can send RECN updates. If you email support, we receive your email address, message, and any attachments you choose to send. Please avoid sending private recordings or other sensitive information unless needed for your request.</p>
      <p>RECN does not include advertising or an advertising SDK. We use the information described here to provide the requested features, respond to support requests, send requested updates, and diagnose problems.</p>

      <h2>Retention and deletion</h2>
      <p>Your local library remains on your devices until you delete it or remove the app's data. You can delete recordings and notes in RECN. Check paired devices, exported files, and operating-system backups separately: deleting the app or a local copy does not necessarily remove those other copies. Device identity stored in secure storage may survive an app reinstall.</p>
      <p>Diagnostic reports are subject to the retention settings of the Sentry project. Support messages are kept to handle and follow up on your request, and update-signup details are kept while you want to receive updates. Email us to request deletion of support or signup information, to stop updates, or to ask about a diagnostic report. We may need information to locate your report because RECN has no account tying reports to your email address.</p>
      <p>We cannot retrieve or remotely delete a library stored only on your device. There is no RECN account to close.</p>

      <h2>Teen users</h2>
      <p>RECN is intended for people aged <strong>13 and over</strong>, including teenagers. It is not directed at children under 13. If you believe a child under 13 has sent us personal information, contact us so we can investigate and remove it where applicable.</p>

      <h2>Service providers and changes</h2>
      <p>The services mentioned above may process information in countries other than yours. Their privacy information is available from <a href="https://sentry.io/privacy/">Sentry</a>, <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub</a>, <a href="https://formspree.io/legal/privacy-policy/">Formspree</a>, and <a href="https://huggingface.co/privacy">Hugging Face</a>. Google Play, Apple, and any apps you use to share files have their own privacy practices.</p>
      <p>We will update this page when RECN's data practices change and revise the date above. Contact <a href="mailto:sinhashubham472@gmail.com">sinhashubham472@gmail.com</a> with questions about this policy or your information.</p>
    </article>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>

<style>
  .privacy-policy { max-width: 70ch; margin-top: 3rem; color: var(--ink); }
  .privacy-policy a { overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
</style>
